### 🚨 Severity: MEDIUM | Security & Architecture Audit

**Root Cause (JAVASCRIPT):** Incorrect Type Conversion can lead to unexpected behaviour and security risks in JavaScript.

**Exploit / Failure Scenario:** Untrusted input or unsafe state handling in the incoming PR diff allows an attacker or malformed payload to trigger the vulnerability above.

**Drop-in Patched Code:**
```javascript
function login(username, password){
    const users = {'admin': 'password', 'user': '123456'};
    const userPassword = users[username];

    // Check if the user exists in the users object
    if(typeof userPassword !== 'undefined') {
        // Use === operator instead of == to avoid type conversion
        if(userPassword === password){
            console.log('Login Successful');
        } else {
            console.log('Login Failed');
        }
    } else {
        console.log('User does not exist');
    }
}

login('admin', 'password');
```

